claim:
The .tt and .cs templates diverge in TransformUtilities. The hunk changes the nesting-type brace emission from `anyConstraints ? "{" : " {
"` to `hasConstraints ? "{
" : " {
"`. This changes the generated output for every formatter nested in a generic type with constraints, even though it has nothing to do with the coverage attribute. Users who check in generated output or snapshot it will see a whitespace diff. The compiled code is semantically the same, but the change is outside the requirement's scope and shows up as a diff in generated files.

